<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8414" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cistŏphŏrus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏs</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιστοφόρος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The bearer of the sacred box</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			2318</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An Asiatic coin of the value of about four
			drachms</i>, <i>on which a</i> cista <i>was stamped</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 2, 6, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 16,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Dom. 20,
				52</span></i>.—<i>Gen. plur.</i>
			cistophorūm, <i><span class="en">Liv. 37, 46, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">39, 7, 1</span></i>; Paul. ex
				<i><span class="en">Fest. p. 78</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
